[1mHow I handled the UB (not a bug fix):[22m I built the C with the shipped [38;5;10mCMakeLists.txt[0m settings (no [38;5;10mCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE[0m, so unoptimized) and found [38;5;10mbad()[0m deterministically prints [38;5;10m0[0m — 20/20 runs. The translation reproduces that via a named [38;5;10mUNINITIALIZED_POINTER_READ[0m constant so the value's provenance is explicit rather than looking like real logic. Worth knowing: this is build-dependent. At [38;5;10m-O1[0m and above the same source segfaults (rc 139), so byte-identical output holds against the unoptimized reference build, not against every possible compilation of UB.[0m[0m
